- [N2] Omitted trace (input 2): i1:To start the process for ACME, begin with the New Resupply Cycle and then Check Levels of Inventory. -> i2:If the inventory is below or equal to the minimum, generate an Equal to or below minimum Report. If the inventory is greater than the minimum, generate an Above Minimum Report. -> i3:If the report indicates that the inventory is equal to or below the minimum, create Purchase Orders (POs). -> i6:If the PO is created, it needs to be reviewed. -> i5:If the PO is rejected, it needs to be reworked. If the PO is approved, it is printed and released in the system. -> i7:Simultaneously, reserve funds for the released POs and mail the POs to the supplier. -> i8:If funds are reserved for the released POs, receive the Packing Slip. If the POs are mailed to the supplier, receive the inventory. -> i9:If the Packing Slip is received, proceed to receive the Invoice. If the inventory is received, proceed to receive the Packing Slip. -> i10:If the Invoice is received, proceed to the Three-way match. -> i11:If the Three-way match is successful, release the funds. -> i12:Once the funds are released, issue the payment. -> i13:After the payment is issued, the Resupply Cycle is complete and the process ends.

